cff-version: 1.2.0
# このリポジトリはサイトの生成器であって研究成果ではない。引用対象として掲げない。
# 引用すべきは各業種のベンチと方法論の論文（NOTICE にDOIの一覧がある）。
# 2026-08-19 に一度 Zenodo でDOIを発行してしまった（10.5281/zenodo.22002590）。
# 発行済みDOIは取り消せないので、掲げるのをやめることで扱いを揃える。
message: "引用する場合は、このサイトではなく各業種のベンチか方法論の論文（NOTICE 参照）を引用してください。"
type: software

title: "monosashi.work: 撤回文を一文字も持たずに撤回を出す公開サイト"

abstract: >-
  The public face of an index that measures, with one common yardstick, how far
  AI reaches into the actual work of licensed professions. The measurements
  themselves live in per-profession benchmark repositories; this repository
  holds only the site text and its generator.

  Its design point is retraction. Benchmarks keep issuing versions and sometimes
  retract results. If the site copies that prose, the same sentence exists in two
  places and one of them rots. So this repository stores **no retraction text at
  all**. The authority is each benchmark's own `.zenodo.json` (the change
  paragraphs) and `CITATION.cff` (version and DOI); the build reads them, compares
  the version an article was written against with the current version, and splices
  the intervening paragraphs in verbatim. Summarising them would reintroduce the
  duplication it exists to prevent.

  Two fields are kept separate on purpose: `version` is what the article
  corresponds to (a fact, shown to readers) and `acknowledged` is how far a human
  has read and judged (a decision, the basis of the gate). Merging them makes
  "deployed while the version gap is disclosed" inexpressible. The gate returns a
  non-zero exit code rather than failing the build, so that spliced content can be
  read before it is acknowledged — failing the build would invert the order and
  require acknowledging in order to see what is being acknowledged. A nightly
  `--check` covers drift during periods with no deploy, which the build-time gate
  cannot see.

  職種ごとにAIが実務をどこまでやれるかを同じ物差しで測って公開する
  「AI実務到達度インデックス」の公開面。**撤回文を1文字も置かない**構造で、
  正本は各ベンチの .zenodo.json と CITATION.cff にしかない。

